# Expectation record for 06_control_flow/009_recursion_call_chains.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 009_recursion_call_chains
area               = 06_control_flow
description        = Direct recursion, a branching call tree, two mutual-recursion pairs, a recursion keeping values live across the call, a recursion holding a local array live across the call, and a recursion dispatching through a switch, all at bounded shallow depth
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Free of undefined and unspecified behaviour, and bounded by design.

The recursion bound is 31 frames. The deepest chain is sum_to(30), which
occupies 31 frames counting the base case. Every other chain is shallower:
is_odd(21) reaches 22 frames, is_even(20) reaches 21, fib(15) reaches depth 15,
ping(10) and pong(10) reach 11, fact(10) reaches 10, and switched(10) and
frames(5) each reach 6.

What this program asserts is the RESULT of each bounded recursion and each call
chain, and nothing about how the calls are implemented. No frame, no prologue or
epilogue, no argument register, no spill and no symbol is required to exist: a
backend is free to inline every helper, fold a whole recursion to a constant,
turn self-recursion into a loop, or discard a function's symbol entirely, and
every line below is still expected to be identical. This suite's oracles compare
stdout bytes and exit status, so a transformation that changes the call structure
while preserving the values is not a divergence at all.
The depths were nevertheless chosen deliberately, as motivation for the shapes
rather than as a claim about generated code. A depth of 31 is large enough that a
backend which does emit frames has to pass arguments, propagate return values and
keep live state across a call; chain keeps two values live across its recursive
call and frames keeps a fully written eight-element local array live across its
own, which is the shape that would exercise callee-saved preservation on such a
backend. The depths are also small enough that every cell completes promptly
inside the per-cell time budget -- fib stops at 15, so its tree of 1973 calls
finishes instantly under emulation -- and small enough to be unremarkable for any
plausible execution environment whether or not the recursion survives
translation. The repository's own runtime-verified recursion depths are single
digit (factorial(5) and fib(7)), so these bounds stay in the same order of
magnitude.

No signed overflow is possible. Every bound was chosen against the 32-bit int
range that all four targets share: the largest value produced anywhere is
3628800, which is 10 factorial. fib stops at 15 so the tree of 1973 calls
completes instantly under emulation and inside the per-cell time budget. Every
recursion has a reachable base case for every argument actually passed, and no
negative argument is ever passed. The local array in frames is fully written by
a loop before the early return and before any element is read, so no
indeterminate storage is ever read; it is automatic storage, never dynamically
allocated. There are no shifts, no pointer arithmetic and no type punning,
therefore no aliasing violation and no dependence on padding bytes. No object is
modified twice between sequence points. The multi-argument printf calls pass
only calls to pure helper functions that read no mutable global, write no global
and touch no volatile object, so although their relative evaluation order is
unspecified it is unobservable and no dependence on unspecified order exists.
Each volatile object is read exactly once per use.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
Nothing implementation-defined is observed. Only int values are printed, so the
measured plain-char signedness difference (signed on x86_64 and i686, unsigned
on aarch64 and riscv64) cannot affect the output, and the measured width
difference for long and pointers (4 bytes on i686, 8 elsewhere) is never exposed
because no long, pointer, size_t or ptrdiff_t value is printed and no sizeof
result appears in the output. int is 32 bits on all four targets, and every
computed value including the negative intermediate in chain lies far inside that
range. No address is printed. No floating point is used. The four backends
implement four different application binary interfaces, and chain and frames are
shaped to keep values live across a recursive call, which is the shape that would
exercise callee-saved preservation on any backend that emits frames for them.
What is compared is the resulting values, not the mechanism: a backend that
inlines the recursion away is as acceptable as one that spills, and either way a
difference in the printed values would be a genuine defect rather than an
implementation-defined difference. All four targets and all three optimization
levels are therefore compared, and all three oracles are enabled.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
const_fact=1 120 3628800
runtime_fact_one=1
runtime_fact_ten=3628800
const_fib=0 1 13 610
runtime_fib_seven=13
runtime_fib_fifteen=610
const_sum_to=0 55 465
runtime_sum_to_zero=0
runtime_sum_to_thirty=465
const_mutual_parity=1 1 0 1
runtime_is_even_twenty=1
runtime_is_odd_twentyone=1
const_ping_pong=0 15 15
runtime_ping_ten=15
runtime_pong_ten=15
const_chain=0 -4 5
runtime_chain_ten=5
const_frames=0 260
runtime_frames_five=260
const_switched=0 1 30
runtime_switched_ten=30
END
